Z||000005||batboy||06-25-2000||01:46 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/airflow.jpg"> <P>Here's what Stetz was trying to post. That idea will help with the air pooling up under the hood, which contributes to high speed lif. Will it help much with cooling, I don't know. The reason the hood scoops or louvers work good is that hot air exits these vents and escapes over the top of the car. Without the top louvers, the radiator heated air had to go under the car where it's sucked up into the engine compartment to help cool the motor. If the air reaching the engine compartment is cooler, then that's a very good thing.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 06-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||06-25-2000||02:01 PM||||bb--That's very artistic. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
